## Auth Flow — How It Works Now

```
App boots
  → Load disclaimer → Load Login screen (if no JWT in localStorage)
    → User enters password → POST /api/login
      → Backend validates against KINGIN_USER_PASSWORD in .env
        → Returns JWT + controlToken
          → Stored in localStorage as 'kingin_jwt' and 'kingin_ctrl'
            → App renders Dashboard
              → All /api/engine/* calls attach Bearer token automatically
              
Token expires / 401 received:
  → api.js interceptor clears localStorage tokens
  → Dispatches 'kingin:unauthorized' DOM event
  → App.jsx listener sets isAuthenticated = false
  → Login screen re-appears (no full page reload)

Switching accounts:
  → User goes to Settings → "Switch Account" (or System panel logout)
  → handleLogout() clears tokens, sets isAuthenticated = false
  → Login screen appears
  → User logs in again
  → Setup Wizard shown if config is incomplete
```

